# NUC-24: per-job override for agent_propose.sh (AGENT_JOB_OVERRIDES). Non-secret
# task wiring only — API keys stay in the canonical secrets.env, sourced first.
#
# EXAMPLE ONLY. The live file lives OUTSIDE git at
#   ~/.config/agent-workforce/weekly_pre_assembly.env  (mode 600, owned by dave)
# and is intentionally NOT committed — mirrors m1_signal_scan.env exactly.
# Install: copy the vars below into that path, then chmod 600.
#
# 2026-07-28: runtime swapped from hermes/claudius (OpenRouter) to headless Claude
# Code (Sonnet, box subscription). This job was the one left behind by the 2026-07-24
# budget pause that moved m1-signal-scan across, and its first run after that pause
# (Fri 2026-07-24 22:04) failed three times on
#   HTTP 402: ... requested up to 65536 tokens, but can only afford 15227
# OpenRouter reserves the worst-case cost of max_tokens up front, so a nearly spent
# monthly cap rejects the request before any inference happens — nothing about the
# job itself was broken. agent_propose.sh is runtime-agnostic (it just execs
# AGENT_RUNTIME_CMD), so only these lines change. To revert to claudius/OpenRouter:
# restore the .bak of the live file (requires OpenRouter headroom).
AGENT_PROFILE=claude-sonnet
AGENT_TASK_SLUG=weekly-pre-assembly
# Optional: cap retries so a transient failure doesn't triple-run an expensive
# Claude Code pass (default is 3).
AGENT_MAX_ATTEMPTS=2
AGENT_RUNTIME_CMD='~/agent-workforce/bin/run_weekly_pre_assembly_cc.sh'

# --- Previous runtime (hermes/claudius on OpenRouter), kept for easy revert ---
# AGENT_TASK_SLUG=weekly-pre-assembly
# AGENT_RUNTIME_CMD='cd ~/agent-worktrees/inbox && ~/.local/bin/hermes -z "$(cat ~/agent-workforce/profiles/weekly_pre_assembly_task.md)" -p claudius'
